To generate similar plots using Bokeh, follow these steps:

1. Import the required libraries and load your dataset.
2. Create a Bokeh plot with the desired layout and tools.
3. Add a ColumnDataSource to the plot with the necessary data.
4. Define a JavaScript callback function to update the plot when the user selects a country or radio button.
5. Attach the callback function to the relevant events.
6. Display the plot using the `show` function.

Here's an example code snippet based on your given dataset:

```python
import pandas as pd
from bokeh.plotting import figure, show
from bokeh.layouts import column, widgetbox
from bokeh.models import ColumnDataSource, Select, RadioButtonGroup, Div, HoverTool
from bokeh.events import ButtonClick

# Load your dataset
df = pd.read_csv("your_dataset.csv")

# Create a Bokeh plot with the desired layout and tools
p = figure(title="Bokeh COVID-19 Data Explorer", x_axis_label="Review Time", y_axis_label="Accurate Star")
p.toolbar.active_drag = "box_zoom"
p.toolbar.active_inspect = True

# Add a ColumnDataSource to the plot with the necessary data
source = ColumnDataSource(df)

# Define a JavaScript callback function to update the plot when the user selects a country or radio button
callback = CustomJS(args=dict(source=source), code="""
    var country = select.value;
    var radio_button = radio.active;
    var data = source.data;

    // Filter the data based on the selected country or radio button
    if (country) {
        data = data[data['country'] == country];
    } else if (radio_button) {
        data = data[data['radio_button'] == radio_button];
    }

    // Update the plot with the filtered data
    source.data = data;
    source.change.emit();
