3. Implement Distributed Communication:
Implement distributed communication using standard protocols such as HTTP or SOAP. This allows your web service to communicate with other systems over a network.
4. Add Self-Description Capabilities:
Add self-description capabilities to your web service by providing a WSDL (Web Services Description Language) file that describes the interface and operations of your web service. This allows clients to discover and understand your web service without needing to know its implementation details.
5. Modularize Your Code:
Modularize your code by breaking it down into smaller, reusable components. This makes it easier to maintain and update your web service, and allows you to reuse code across multiple projects.

