Note that the brute force algorithm has a time complexity of O(n^3), which can be slow for large arrays. Therefore, more efficient algorithms like sorting or hashing are often used to solve this problem.

To set up a Docker Compose server with Nginx, Let's Encrypt Certbot, PHP 8.1, and MariaDB, you will need the following files and configurations:

1. Docker Compose file (docker-compose.yml):

```yaml
version: '3'
services:
  nginx:
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
      - "80:80"
      - "443:443"
    volumes:
      - ./nginx/conf.d:/etc/nginx/conf.d
      - ./nginx/html:/usr/share/nginx/html
    depends_on:
      - php
      - mariadb
  php:
    image: php:8.1-fpm
    volumes:
      - ./php:/var/www/html
    depends_on:
      - mariadb
  mariadb:
    image: mariadb:10.6
    environment:
      - MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=password
      - MYSQL_DATABASE=database
      - MYSQL_USER=username
      - MYSQL_PASSWORD=password
    volumes:
      - ./mariadb:/var/lib/mysql
```

2. Nginx configuration file (nginx/conf.d/default.conf):

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name example.com;

    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.php index.html index.htm;
    }

    location ~ \.php$ {
        fastcgi_pass php:9000;
        fastcgi_index index.php;
        include fastcgi_params;
    }

    location ~ /\.well-known {
        allow all;
    }
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name example.com;

    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl

