Here's a simple code snippet that demonstrates how to check if a website is accessible using JavaScript:

```javascript
function isWebsiteAccessible(url) {
  const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
  xhr.open('HEAD', url, true);
  xhr.send();

  return xhr.status === 200;
}

const websiteUrl = 'https://example.com';

if (isWebsiteAccessible(websiteUrl)) {
  console.log('Access granted');
} else {
  console.log('Access denied');
}
```

This code uses the XMLHttpRequest object to send a HEAD request to the specified website URL. If the request is successful (status code 200), it means the website is accessible. Otherwise, it means the website is unavailable.

