Alternatively, you can use a proxy server or a reverse proxy to handle the requests and add the authorization header before forwarding the requests to your server. This way, the proxy server acts as an intermediary between the client and the server, and it can add the authorization header to the requests based on the client's authentication credentials.

Here's an example of how you can configure Nginx as a proxy server to add the authorization header:
```
server {
    listen 80;
