Here's an R function that checks if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
# Function to check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric
is_all_numeric <- function(x) {
  # Check if the input is a character vector
  stopifnot(is.character(x))

  # Initialize a logical vector to store the result for each element
  result <- FALSE

  # Loop through each element in the character vector
  for (i in seq_along(x)) {
    # Try to convert the current element to numeric
    tryCatch({
      x[i] <- as.numeric(x[i])
      result[i] <- TRUE
    }, error = function(e) {
      result[i] <- FALSE
    })
  }

  # Return the final result
  return(result)
}
```

To use this function, simply call it with your character vector as an argument:

```R
# Example usage
x <- c("1", "2", "3", "4", "5", "6")
is_all_numeric(x)
```

This will return `TRUE`, indicating that all non-NA elements in the vector `x` can be converted to numeric. If any element cannot be converted to numeric, the function will return `FALSE`.

