To achieve this task, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Install Accord.NET NuGet package
2. Load and preprocess the dataset
3. Create a Naive Bayes classifier
4. Train the classifier on the preprocessed dataset
5. Predict the label for a new sentence

Here's a concise and elegant C# code that accomplishes this task:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text;
using Accord.MachineLearning;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Classification;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Transformations;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Load and preprocess the dataset
        var dataset = LoadDataset("dataset.csv");
        var preprocessor = new TextPreprocessing(new[] { StopWordsRemover.English });
        var transformedDataset = preprocessor.Transform(dataset);

        // Create a Naive Bayes classifier
        var classifier = new NaiveBayes();

        // Train the classifier on the preprocessed dataset
        classifier.Train(transformedDataset);

        // Predict the label for a new sentence
        var newSentence = "The sports game was exciting";
        var prediction = classifier.Predict(new[] { newSentence });
        Console.WriteLine($"Predicted label: {prediction}");
    }

    private static Dataset LoadDataset(string filePath)
    {
        var dataset = new Dataset(filePath, hasHeaders: true);
        return dataset;
    }
}
```

Make sure to replace `"dataset.csv"` with the path to your dataset file. This code will load the dataset, preprocess it, create a Naive Bayes classifier, train the classifier on the preprocessed dataset, and predict the label for a new sentence.

