To create a socket for chat rooms, you'll need to use a server-side language like PHP along with a library like Socket.IO or Swoole. In this example, I'll demonstrate how to use Socket.IO with PHP.

First, install Socket.IO using Composer by running the following command:
```bash
composer require socketio/socket.io-client
```
Next, create a new PHP file named `server.php` and add the following code:
```php
<?php
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';

use Ratchet\Server\IoServer;
use Ratchet\Http\HttpServer;
use Ratchet\WebSocket\WsServer;
use Ratchet\Client\WebSocketClient;

class ChatServer extends IoServer
{
    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct(
            new HttpServer(
                new WsServer(
                    new WebSocketClient('ws://localhost:3000')
                )
            )
        );
    }

    protected function onConnect($conn)
    {
        echo "New client connected\n";
    }

    protected function onMessage($conn, $msg)
    {
        echo "Received message: {$msg}\n";

        // Broadcast the message to all connected clients
        foreach ($this->connections as $connection) {
            $connection->send($msg);
        }
    }

    protected function onClose($conn)
    {
        echo "Client disconnected\n";
    }
}

$server = new ChatServer();
$server->run();
```
