To create an iOS shortcut that identifies and deletes user files that have not been accessed in over 3 years, follow these steps:

1. Open the "Shortcuts" app on your iPhone.
2. Tap on the "+" icon to create a new shortcut.
3. Name your shortcut, for example, "Delete Old Files."
4. Add the following actions to the shortcut:
   - "Ask for Input" action: This action will prompt you to select the folder or file type you want to delete.
   - "Get Contents of Folder" action: This action will list all the files and folders in the selected directory.
   - "Filter Files" action: This action will filter the files based on their modification date. Set the date range to "3 years ago" to only include files that have not been accessed in over 3 years.
   - "Delete Files" action: This action will delete the selected files.
5. Customize the shortcut by adding more actions or adjusting the existing ones as needed.
6. Test the shortcut by running it on your device. Make sure it works as expected before using it to delete important files.

